<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap g2">
    <article class="card feature">
      <span class="eyebrow">Vocabulary</span>
      <h3 class="px">brand your words</h3>
      <p>
        Say a word five times; Voice Pipes replays each take 30 ways through Parakeet and rounds up every way it got it
        wrong, and with a Jev key, Jev flags which ones are safe to replace everywhere. Fix words then swaps them on your
        Mac, instantly. No model is retrained.
      </p>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="term-body"><span class="c-muted">i asked</span> <span class="struck">cloud code</span> <span class="c-green">Claude Code</span> <span class="c-muted">to set up</span> <span class="struck">open router</span> <span class="c-green">OpenRouter</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature">
      <span class="eyebrow">History</span>
      <h3 class="px">no steer left behind</h3>
      <p>
        Clicked away mid-sentence? The paste went nowhere? Your last 1,000 takes stay in History. Open one for every
        step: its time and output, which branch Jev picked, and what the cloud steps cost. Search them, copy one, paste
        it again.
      </p>
      <div class="card run">
        <div class="run__text">
          <span class="run__meta">Fast dictation · 2 min ago · 142 ms <span class="c-orange">· paste had no field</span></span>
          <span class="run__said">Let's ship the HUD changes in the next release.</span>
        </div>
        <span class="run__badge">Copied ✓</span>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature">
      <span class="eyebrow">Read along</span>
      <h3 class="px">hold the reins</h3>
      <p>
        Anything read aloud, from your selection to an agent's summary, can show as text you follow, a sentence per line
        with the spoken word underlined. Click a sentence to jump there. The HUD takes the keys without taking you out of
        your app.
      </p>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="term-body feature__keys" role="img" aria-label="Illustration: the HUD while reading, with KEYS ON, and its default keys: j and k for the next and previous sentence, h and l for slower and faster, Space to pause, Esc to stop">
          <span class="hud"><span class="sq" style="background: var(--purple)"></span>READ <span class="c-muted">42%</span> <span class="c-purple">KEYS ON</span></span>
          <span class="chain"><span class="key">j k</span><span class="c-muted">sentence</span><span class="key">h l</span><span class="c-muted">speed</span><span class="key">Space</span><span class="c-muted">pause</span><span class="key">Esc</span><span class="c-muted">stop</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature">
      <span class="eyebrow">Model pickers</span>
      <h3 class="px">size up every model</h3>
      <p>
        Every picker shows what a paragraph costs, how fast the model has been on your Mac, and a 1–5 quality rating from
        Artificial Analysis's public leaderboards. Sort by best value, quality, speed or cost; the models on your Mac stay
        on top.
      </p>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="term-body feature__keys" role="img" aria-label="Illustration: a model picker's sort choices, Best value selected, and its columns: paragraph cost, speed and quality">
          <span class="chain"><span class="key c-fg">Best value</span><span class="key">Quality</span><span class="key">Speed</span><span class="key">Cost</span></span>
          <span class="chain"><span class="c-muted">on this Mac first</span><span class="sep">›</span><span class="c-muted">paragraph</span><span class="sep">·</span><span class="c-muted">speed</span><span class="sep">·</span><span class="c-muted">quality</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
